# Cernun

## Lore

Ram-horned serpent men, intelligent creatures of magic. The ram-horned serpent was a major icon of the ancient Celts, especially in Gaul, and it seems likely that the cernun visited Earth long ago and were taken for gods: a ley line nexus in France links to the Cernun dimension, and a powerful cernun may have been Cernunnos, Lord of Animals, symbol of fertility, growth and renewal. A thick body ends in a powerful tail; the arms are thin and human-like, the legs muscular with large clawed feet for climbing. Laid flat on its belly a cernun looks very like a serpent.

## GM Notes

Most cernun are greedy and seek vast wealth, fame or fear, and power, and most are evil sorcerers and a threat to good beings. They are rare on Rifts Earth, fewer than a thousand, most likely met in France, Spain, the British Isles, western Europe, Africa and Atlantis. Gigantes appear to populate their home world and serve them; some suspect the cernun created the mutant giants. They love magic weapons, wands, staves, potions and items. Average NPC level 1D4+3, hand to hand expert or assassin.
